    <item>
      <title>A Prayer to Recharge</title>
      <link>https://appapappa.com/interests/spirituality/prayers/a_prayer_to_recharge/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 16 Nov 2025 06:51:41 +0530</pubDate>
      <guid>https://appapappa.com/interests/spirituality/prayers/a_prayer_to_recharge/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;by-paramahansa-yogananda&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  By Paramahansa Yogananda&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#by-paramahansa-yogananda&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;“Heavenly Father, it is Thou&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Who dost directly sustain my body.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Awaken within me&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Conscious will, conscious health,&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Conscious vitality, conscious realization.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;O Eternal Youth of body and mind!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Abide in me forever and forever”&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Buddhir Balam</title>
      <link>https://appapappa.com/interests/spirituality/prayers/buddhir_balam/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 16 Nov 2025 06:51:41 +0530</pubDate>
      <guid>https://appapappa.com/interests/spirituality/prayers/buddhir_balam/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-first-prayer-my-mother-taught-me&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  The first prayer my mother taught me&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#the-first-prayer-my-mother-taught-me&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;“Buddhir balam&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Yasho dhairyam!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Nirbhayathvam&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Arogatha!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Ajaatyam&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Vaakpadudhvamsa&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Hanumadh&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Smaranaath bhaveth”&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;बुद्धि (buddhi) — intelligence, बलम् (balam) — strength, यश् (yash) — fame, धैर्यम् (dhairyam) — courage, निर्भयत्वम् (nirbhayatvam) — fearlessness, अरोगताम् (arogatAm) — disease-free health, अजाड्यम् (ajADyam) — determination, वाक् पटुत्वम् च​ (vAk paTutvam ca) — and articulateness of speech, will all last forever (भवेत्, bhavet) if you meditate (स्मरणात् , smaraNAt) on Lord Hanuman (हनुमत्, hanumat) at all times.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Mother Teresas Prayer</title>
      <link>https://appapappa.com/interests/spirituality/prayers/mother_teresas_prayer/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 16 Nov 2025 06:51:41 +0530</pubDate>
      <guid>https://appapappa.com/interests/spirituality/prayers/mother_teresas_prayer/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;philosophy-of-the-missionaries-of-charity&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Philosophy of the Missionaries of Charity&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#philosophy-of-the-missionaries-of-charity&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The fruit of silence is prayer&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The fruit of prayer is faith&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The fruit of faith is love&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The fruit of love is service&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The fruit of service is peace&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Tvameva Mata</title>
      <link>https://appapappa.com/interests/spirituality/prayers/tvameva/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 16 Nov 2025 06:51:41 +0530</pubDate>
      <guid>https://appapappa.com/interests/spirituality/prayers/tvameva/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;guru-shloka&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Guru Shloka&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#guru-shloka&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tvam-Eva Maataa Ca Pitaa Tvam-Eva |&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tvam-Eva Bandhush-Ca Sakhaa Tvam-Eva |&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tvam-Eva Viidyaa Dravinnam Tvam-Eva |&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tvam-Eva Sarvam Mama Deva Deva ||&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You Truly are my Mother And You Truly are my Father .&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You Truly are my Relative And You Truly are my Friend.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You Truly are my Knowledge and You Truly are my Wealth.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You Truly are my All, My God of Gods.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
